    pharm: "1. Cardiac protection (IMMEDIATE): IV Calcium Gluconate 10% 10-20mL (or Calcium Chloride 5-10mL) over 2-5 minutes. Repeat in 5 minutes if ECG changes persist. 2. Shift K+ intracellularly (temporary): Nebulised Salbutamol 10-20mg (onset 30 min, reduces K+ by 0.5-1.5). OR IV Insulin 10 units + 50% Dextrose 50mL (onset 15 min, peak 30-60 min). 3. Remove K+ from body: IV Furosemide 40-80mg (if some renal function). KCl-binding resin: Calcium Resonium 15g TID PO/PR. Consider haemodialysis (definitive, if K+ remains >6.5 despite medical therapy). 4. Reverse precipitating factors: STOP Spironolactone. STOP/Hold Losartan (ACEi/ARB). Stop K+-sparing drugs. Review diet. 5. Correct acidosis: IV Sodium Bicarbonate 50-100 mEq (if pH <7.2).",
